  "quality_and_interpretation_rules":["Public catalog metadata is not equivalent to the complete underlying record corpus","A record being classified, withheld, or redacted does not establish its contents","A missing online record does not prove destruction","A records-disposition schedule can authorize destruction; verify current schedule status before interpreting it","An allegation, investigation, arrest, charge, conviction, civil action, and administrative enforcement are distinct legal states","Do not infer criminality from a person's appearance in an archival record","Historical crime statistics may reflect reporting and classification changes rather than true changes in incidence","Financial statistics are not inherently criminal records","Preserve original source and retrieval date for every normalized field"],
  "important_archive_limitations":["NARA states that FBI records in its holdings are generally case files closed before 1985 and that not all FBI classifications or permanent case files have been accessioned","NARA's Record Group Explorer estimates online textual scans from Catalog data and estimated total pages; online availability is therefore not equivalent to complete archival coverage","The 1973 National Personnel Records Center fire destroyed or damaged substantial military personnel records, creating permanent gaps in portions of the historical record"],
